    "result_text": "The AcceptanceTest is the only test class in the suite, and both tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the telephone-uniqueness rule for `POST /api/owners` as a new, cohesive pipeline step rather than modifying any existing function \u2014 keeping structural impact minimal (no existing method changed; new units each carry near-zero surrounding complexity).\n\n**New files:**\n- `CheckUniqueTelephone.java` \u2014 a single-method step that runs after `BuildOwner` (so it sees the normalized 10-digit telephone) and before `SaveOwner`. It scans all owners, normalizes each stored telephone, and throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` on a match with any other owner.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneHandler.java` \u2014 escalation handler responding `409 CONFLICT`.\n- `escalation/\u2026DuplicateTelephoneException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `checkTelephone` step between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe check sits after build (normalized value available) and before save (rejects before persisting), matching the spec: any existing owner sharing the normalized telephone yields a 409.",
